@startuml
title UML - Implemented original-identity recovery and cancellation (WP-23)
autonumber
actor "Owned customer / current payment operator" as User
boundary "BFF / recovery API" as API
control "Payments" as Pay
database "Payments store" as Store
control "Platform leased job" as Job
control "Core" as Core
participant "Synthetic rail" as Rail
control "Controls cases / audit" as Controls

User -> API : Cancellation, or operator inquiry with exact reason + request key
API -> Pay : Current ownership / operator role / queue; origin + CSRF
Pay -> Store : Lock original intent; seal command identity and digest
Pay -> Store : Commit acceptance before scheduling
Pay -> Job : Accept same command ID; bounded original recovery job
API --> User : 202 accepted, financial outcome unconfirmed

Job -> Pay : Original request ID and original payment
Pay -> Core : Recover committed booking / finality receipt first
alt Existing finality or booking receipt
 Core --> Pay : Original immutable financial result
 Pay -> Store : Repair workflow and command from original receipt
else Cancellation before possible submission
 Pay -> Store : Same intent lock as execution; cancellation already durable
 Pay -> Core : Release exact bound unsubmitted reservation if present
 Pay -> Store : CANCELLED; no provider send
else Submitted inquiry or cancellation
 Pay -> Store : Read exact original work; claim short fenced lease
 Pay -> Store : Commit before transport; defer if existing lease is active
 Pay -> Rail : Signed original identity + full original scope
 alt Timeout / pending / NOT_FOUND
  Rail --> Pay : Unknown or nonfinal result
  Pay -> Store : Retain original submitted commitment
  Pay -> Job : Bounded retry; exhaustion requires owned review
  Pay -> Controls : Owned payment case; no expiry release
 else Matching final evidence
  Rail --> Pay : Original SETTLED / REJECTED / CANCELLED packet
  Pay -> Store : Recheck lease / fence after locks; immutable receipt
  Pay -> Core : Independently verify evidence; same financial business key
  alt Settlement already committed
   Core --> Pay : Same settlement journal; cancellation too late
  else Definitive nonexecution
   Core -> Core : Release submitted hold and daily budget atomically
   Core --> Pay : Immutable release / finality receipt
  end
  Pay -> Store : Canonical financial status + immutable command history
 end
end

group Periodic bounded reconciliation
 Pay -> Store : Claim persistent cursor page (50); commit cursor before service work
 Pay -> Core : Read authoritative reservation / hold / booking / daily-use positions
 Core --> Pay : Financial snapshot, including computed aggregate held amount
 Pay -> Store : Compare owning intent, scope, provider work, finality and age
 alt Orphan / mismatch / submitted age >= synthetic 5 minute threshold
  Pay -> Store : Stable break ID; append changed observation; durable audit
  Pay -> Controls : Idempotent owned case with original financial identity
 else Previously observed break now matches
  Pay -> Store : MATCHED observation + retained history
  note right of Controls
  Matching preserves the investigation.
  No financial override or automatic case closure.
  end note
 end
end
User -> API : Scoped inquiry and recovery history
API --> User : Financial result, pending cancellation or owned reconciliation evidence
note over Pay,Core
Recovery never mints another economic payment.
Unknown submitted funds cannot expire into release.
Late cancellation preserves the original settlement.
end note
@enduml
